# NOTICE — hermes-imagegen

This project is a **port** of [dickpy/dsh-imagegen](https://github.com/dickpy/dsh-imagegen)
(version 1.18.1, Apache-2.0) from the DeepSeek Harness (DSH) web GUI to the
Hermes Desktop plugin platform.

## What was reused

- The model-family catalog and per-provider request shaping tables
  (`src/model-catalog.ts`, `effectiveParams()` / `effectiveCount()` in
  `src/engine.ts`) — ported to `dashboard/imagegen_backend/models.py`, tables
  copied verbatim so provider wire formats do not drift.
- The upstream response-handling rules in `src/engine.ts`: base64/URL result
  normalisation, the same-origin rule for forwarding the Bearer on result
  downloads, async `task_id` polling on `/tasks/{id}`, and the stable error
  codes (`config-missing`, `upstream-rejected`, `mask-size-mismatch`, …).
- The multi-reference upload convention (`image[]` repeated, mask as PNG
  matching the first reference's pixel size).

## What was rewritten

- The host integration: DSH's cordis plugin, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` client
  packages, host settings seam and route family have no analogue here, so the
  backend is a FastAPI router (`/api/plugins/hermes-imagegen/`) and the UI is a
  Hermes Desktop plugin.
- The generation queue: an in-process asyncio job registry plus a SQLite
  history store, instead of the DSH host's task queue.
- **Not ported, by decision:** the PNG-to-editable-PPT pipeline (the owner
  does not want pptx output), subscription channels (vendor OAuth logins —
  the mechanism is worthless without the third-party accounts), and the
  upstream canvas extras: sketch boards, vision layer splitting, brush masks,
  annotation edits, file nodes and canvas skills.

## Vendored upstream stylesheet

`design/panel.module.css` is a verbatim copy of the upstream panel stylesheet
(`src/client/panel.module.css`, Apache-2.0, Copyright the dsh-imagegen
authors). `design/studio-results.module.css`, `design/image-action-menu.module.css`
and `design/generation-loading.module.css` are verbatim copies of the matching
upstream CSS modules (`src/client/*.module.css`, same licence and copyright) —
the generation board, its right-click menu and the waiting animation. They are
vendored — not rewritten — so `scripts/build_panel_css.py` can regenerate
`desktop/panel.css`, `panel-results.css`, `panel-menu.css` and
`panel-loading.css` reproducibly in CI: the script scopes every selector under
the sheet's own surface root, maps the `--dsw-alias-*` tokens onto Hermes app
tokens and prefixes keyframes. Each sheet gets a separate root (`.ig-root`,
`.ig-results`, `.ig-menu`, `.ig-loading`) because upstream class names collide
once they stop being hashed. Re-run the script after replacing a vendored file;
CI fails if a generated file drifts.

The result-board row table in `desktop/plugin.js` (`planResultLayout`) is a
port of the upstream `src/client/result-layout.ts` — the same fixed sheet
(1 full, 2 split, 3 as two-over-one, 4 as 2×2, …), checked by
`scripts/check_result_layout.mjs`.

## Bundled prompt-template snapshots

`dashboard/imagegen_backend/templates_data/` ships five case-list snapshots
(≈2,460 cases, JSON only — no image binaries) taken from these projects:

- **yang0/handraw-style** — https://github.com/yang0/handraw-style — MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 yang0
- **andy7076/image_prompt** — https://github.com/andy7076/image_prompt — MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 andy7076
- **EvoLinkAI/awesome-gpt-image-2-prompts** —
  https://github.com/EvoLinkAI/awesome-gpt-image-2-prompts — CC0 1.0 Universal
- **vibeui** gallery JSON (mirror of awesome-gpt-image-2) —
  https://vibeui.top/ — fetched from the site's published `cases.json`
- **canghe** gallery JSON — https://gpt-image2.canghe.ai/ — fetched from the
  site's published `cases.json`

Reference images are **not** bundled: they are fetched on demand from the source
each case names, cached under `~/.hermes/imagegen/template-images/<source>/`, and
served from that cache afterwards. Only hosts pinned per source are allowed.

